<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco raises Gulf ports bunker fuel by $3/t.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco raises Gulf ports bunker fuel by $3/t.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has raised the price of A-960 bunker fuel by $3 a tonne to $127 ($19.49 a barrel) from Gulf ports and cut by $1 a tonne to $127 ($19.49) from Red Sea ports, the firm said.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel grade is also raised by $1 to $224 from Ras Tanura and Dammam though liftings from Jeddah and Yanbu are left unchanged at $225 a tonne.</p>
<p>Prices are effective November 27.</p>
</text>
